Subject: [PATCH] Exit on load failure when supervised

An unattended kiosk must not remain on a manual "Try again" page when the
local application has not started yet. Allow the systemd supervisor to
restart Cog and repeat its HTTP readiness check. Ignore navigation
cancellations as before; normal Cog sessions retain their error page.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [project kiosk supervision policy]

--- a/core/cog-webkit-utils.c
+++ b/core/cog-webkit-utils.c
@@ -92,3 +92,8 @@ cog_handle_web_view_load_failed (WebKitWebView  *web_view,
+    if (g_strcmp0(g_getenv("COG_EXIT_ON_LOAD_FAILURE"), "1") == 0) {
+        g_warning("Kiosk navigation failed for %s: %s", failing_uri, error ? error->message : "unknown error");
+        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);
+    }
+
     return load_error_page (web_view,
                             failing_uri,
                             "Page load error",
